Cross-module [%css] selector interpolation: the PPX emits a sentinel-bearing
CSS rule plus a `[@@@css.refs ...]` descriptor and a synthetic `let _ = M.x`
dependency. The aggregator builds an index across both modules and resolves
the sentinel to the binding id that `M.marker` minted.

  $ refmt --parse re --print ml m.re > m.ml
  $ ../../standalone.exe --impl m.ml -o m.ml
  $ refmt --parse re --print ml n.re > n.ml
  $ ../../standalone.exe --impl n.ml -o n.ml

The post-PPX `n.ml` carries the unresolved sentinel as an opaque NUL-delimited
string in `[@@@css ...]`, plus a `[@@@css.refs ...]` attribute with the
location and a synthetic dep-tracking `let`.

  $ cat n.ml
  [@@@css.atoms
    [("_a4hT1uK_l", ["._a4hT1uK_l{background:red;}"], 1, 0, 9,
       [("value", "T1uK_l", "val\\04h\\0& | \\0background:red")]);
    ("_c4hLsHzqtZno0Ri",
      ["._c4hLsHzqtZno0Ri.\000M.marker\000{background:blue;}"], 2, 1, 9,
      [("ctx", "LsHzqt", "ctx\\0&.$(M.marker)\\0module:N | ");
      ("value", "Zno0Ri",
        "val\\04h\\0&.$(M.marker)\\0module:N | \\0background:blue\\0module:N")]);
    ("_iKLU8Ukj2", [], 1, 0, 0,
      [("id", "_iKLU8Ukj2", "bind\\0\\0N\\0\\0container\\00")])]]
  [@@@css.bindings
    [("N.container", "_iKLU8Ukj2 _a4hT1uK_l _c4hLsHzqtZno0Ri", "_iKLU8Ukj2")]]
  [@@@css.refs [("M.marker", "n.ml", 6, 6, 14)]]
  let _ = M.marker
  let container = CSS.make "_iKLU8Ukj2 _a4hT1uK_l _c4hLsHzqtZno0Ri" []

The aggregator resolves the sentinel against the class minted by `m.ml`.
`M.marker` is an empty `[%css {||}]` so it mints a binding id and emits no rule
of its own; the resolved selector uses that id on the consumer.

  $ styled-ppx.generate m.ml n.ml > styles.css
  $ cat styles.css
  /* This file is generated by styled-ppx, do not edit manually */
  ._a4hT1uK_l{background:red;}
  ._c4hLsHzqtZno0Ri._iVOT1Gbzy{background:blue;}
